============================================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
============================================================

The tool lets a high-school or college student pick a region of Earth, ask
questions about how it is changing over time, and see the answer as a
plain-language "finding" card, a time-series chart, and a spatial trend map.
It has two investigation modes that share the same underlying context:

  CONVERSATION MODE (left: chat, right: artifact cards)
  ANALYST MODE      (left: rail, center: Leaflet map, right: point panel)

Selecting a point on the map and clicking "Discuss this point →" carries
that point into the conversation as the first message. The context (region,
selected point, all cards, all chat messages) persists across mode switches
and page refreshes via localStorage.

This is a hackathon demo. There is NO backend, NO API keys, NO real data
fetch, NO authentication. Everything runs on deterministic mock data seeded
by region slug, so the app looks identical every run. The architecture must
make it obvious where real data/LLM calls would be plugged in later — each
of those places gets a clearly labeled comment.

