RegionMap:
  Props: { region, selectedPoint, onSelectPoint }
  "use client". useEffect imports leaflet dynamically.
  On mount: create Leaflet map centered at region.center, zoom region.zoom,
  add tile layer https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
  with attribution "&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors".
  Draw a 6×8 grid of L.circleMarker across the region bounds. Each marker:
    radius 18, weight 0, fillColor from colorForSlope(), fillOpacity 1.
    On click → onSelectPoint([lat, lng]).
  Map.on("click") also calls onSelectPoint.
  fitBounds(region.bounds, { padding: [16, 16] }).
  A separate useEffect syncs the selected point marker: a circleMarker
  radius 9, weight 2, color --ink, fillColor #fff.
  On cleanup: remove map and all markers.
  The container div has id="leaflet-map", position absolute, inset 0.

  colorForSlope(slope):
    a = min(1, abs(slope) / 1.5)
    if abs(slope) < 0.08: return "rgba(154,163,160,0.55)"
    if slope > 0: return `rgba(194,65,12,${0.25 + a*0.6})`
    else: return `rgba(29,78,216,${0.25 + a*0.6})`

