CHAT BRAIN — lib/chat.ts
============================================================

generateReply(userText, region, stats): { text: string; cardKind: CardKind }
  A simple keyword router. Mark clearly:
  "REPLACE THIS FUNCTION WITH A REAL LLM CALL LATER — the UI contract is
   { text: string, cardKind: CardKind } and nothing else."

  Rules in this priority order (first match wins), all case-insensitive:
    /where|map|distribution|spatial|where is/
      → slope-map, text: "Here's the spatial picture of {shortName}
        trend across {region.name}. Orange = increasing, blue = decreasing.
        Click any point to investigate it individually."
    /what is|explain|define|meaning|what does.*mean/
      → variable, text: "{variable.name} — {variable.description}"
    /significan|caveat|trust|confiden|p-value|p value|reliable|how sure/
      → caveat, text: "The trend here has {formatP(pValue)}.
        {stats.significant ? 'That clears the conventional 0.05 threshold —
        so we can be fairly confident it's real.' : "That's above the 0.05
        threshold, so we can't confidently call this significant yet."}
        Let me lay out what that does and doesn't mean."
    /show|chart|graph|series|over time|plot|data/
      → trend-chart, text: "Here is the full monthly series for
        {shortName} over {region.name}, with the fitted linear trend and
        95% confidence band."
    /trend|changing|change|warmer|cooler|increas|decreas|warming|cooling/
      → finding, text: "Across {region.name}, {shortName} is changing at
        {formatSlope(stats)} ({formatP}). {stats.significant ? 'Statistically
        significant.' : 'Not statistically significant at the conventional
        threshold.'}"
    fallback → finding, text: "Good question. Here's the headline:
      {shortName} over {region.name} has been changing at {formatSlope} ({p}).
      Want me to show the chart, the map, or explain what 'significant'
      means here?"

