============================================================
CONTEXT — lib/context.tsx
============================================================

Client component. Exports InvestigationProvider and useInvestigation().

State shape:
  hydrated: boolean
  region: Region | null
  point: [number, number] | null
  pendingPrompt: string | null
  cards: CanvasCard[]
  messages: ChatMessage[]

Actions:
  setRegion(r) — if r is null, also clear point, cards, messages.
  setPoint(p)
  setPendingPrompt(s)
  addCard(input) — assigns id "card-{timestamp}-{rand}" and createdAt,
                   appends to cards, RETURNS the created card.
  addMessage(input) — assigns id "msg-{timestamp}-{rand}", appends,
                      RETURNS the created message.
  resetRegion()

Persistence:
  STORAGE_KEY = "etd.investigation.v1"
  On mount: read localStorage, hydrate region/point/cards/messages,
            set hydrated true.
  On any change to region/point/cards/messages AND hydrated: write
    { region, point, cards, messages } back to localStorage.

IMPORTANT: always provide the useInvestigation() hook with a runtime guard
that throws if used outside the provider.

Provide the provider in app/layout.tsx so it wraps {children}.

============================================================
ROUTING RULES
============================================================

Each route that depends on [slug] must, on mount:
  - if !hydrated, do nothing
  - getRegion(slug) — if missing, router.replace("/regions")
  - if region?.slug !== slug, setRegion(the found region)

This means the app works whether the user arrives via a card click or by
typing the URL directly, and it survives page refreshes.

